From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] procd: keep the cgroup of an instance that runs again

procd removed an instance's cgroup, and its service's, as soon as the
instance's process had exited, before it started the instance again for
a restart or a respawn. What the init script had set on the service's
cgroup went with it: honk's init pins honk to the big cores through the
cpuset of honk's service cgroup, and after `/etc/init.d/honk restart`
honk ran on every core, in a services/honk procd had just created
(seen on the emulator: cpuset.cpus 4-5 while the old honk exited, empty
once the new one ran).

Carry the procd patch that removes the cgroups only with the instance,
as instance_free already does. It is meant for procd upstream.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 package/system/procd/Makefile                 |  2 +-
 ...group-of-an-instance-that-runs-again.patch | 35 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 36 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 package/system/procd/patches/102-instance-keep-the-cgroup-of-an-instance-that-runs-again.patch

diff --git a/package/system/procd/Makefile b/package/system/procd/Makefile
index 8e383114..9a66dd56 100644
--- a/package/system/procd/Makefile
+++ b/package/system/procd/Makefile
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@
 include $(TOPDIR)/rules.mk
 
 PKG_NAME:=procd
-PKG_RELEASE:=5
+PKG_RELEASE:=6
 
 PKG_SOURCE_PROTO:=git
 PKG_SOURCE_URL=$(PROJECT_GIT)/project/procd.git
diff --git a/package/system/procd/patches/102-instance-keep-the-cgroup-of-an-instance-that-runs-again.patch b/package/system/procd/patches/102-instance-keep-the-cgroup-of-an-instance-that-runs-again.patch
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..3862c8b3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/system/procd/patches/102-instance-keep-the-cgroup-of-an-instance-that-runs-again.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,35 @@
+From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+Subject: [PATCH] instance: keep the cgroup of an instance that runs again
+
+When an instance's process has exited, instance_exit_done removed the
+instance's cgroup and then its service's, before it decided whether the
+instance runs again. A restart (an init script's stop, then a start
+that comes while the old process is still exiting) and a respawn start
+the instance again in a cgroup procd creates anew, and what the init
+script set on its service's cgroup is gone: a cpuset that pins the
+service, the controllers enabled for its instances.
+
+Remove the cgroups only with the instance, as instance_free already
+does when an instance is deleted. An instance that stopped and stays
+registered keeps its empty cgroup, as it keeps a program attached to
+it (instance_set_vrf), until it starts again or is deleted.
+
+Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+---
+ service/instance.c | 3 ---
+ 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)
+
+diff --git a/service/instance.c b/service/instance.c
+index 9c64406..0847c32 100644
+--- a/service/instance.c
++++ b/service/instance.c
+@@ -1423,9 +1423,6 @@ instance_exit_done(struct service_instance *in)
+ 	if (in->proc.pending)
+ 		return;
+ 
+-	if (in->has_cgroup)
+-		instance_rmdir_cgroup(in->srv->name, in->name);
+-
+ 	runtime = in->stop.tv_sec - in->start.tv_sec;
+ 
+ 	if (in->halt) {
